IF - START A CONDITIONAL COMMAND LEVEL

CALLER. Subject to the current caller access policy.

A - Purpose, syntax and examples

:A
IF - START A CONDITIONAL COMMAND LEVEL

CALLER. Subject to the current caller access policy.

Syntax:
    IF condition [arguments]

Starts a conditional level. Commands in a false level are skipped until
the appropriate ELSE or FI. Prefix a supported condition with ~ to negate
it. This installed FCP implements ERROR and NULL internally. NULL is true
when its argument is absent. Other tests, including T/F, need the disk-
based IF.COM; that extension is private and is not on the public A0: path.

Safe example: IF NULL;ECHO TRUE BRANCH;FI

Always balance IF with FI. For extended disk-based tests see HELP IFFILE.
Condition evaluation does not grant access to private files or commands.

See HELP COMMANDS for the command index.
